 ### UI Patterns
 
 - **Orientation**: iPhone is portrait only; iPad supports all four (iPadOS 26 windows resize freely, so portrait-only can't be enforced there). Build settings `INFOPLIST_KEY_UISupportedInterfaceOrientations_*`.
 - **Card grid** (`ScrollView`, not `List`): collapsed cards in rows of 2 (iPhone, or a compact-width iPad window), 3 (iPad portrait) or 4 (iPad landscape / wider than tall); an expanded card takes a full-width row. Multiple cards can be open; expansion is tracked by `CategoryLayoutKey` (name + occurrence) since UUIDs change per week, so open cards persist across week navigation (in memory only). Within a week the grid's `ForEach` is keyed by category ID, so a renamed card stays the same view (a menu, sheet or field open in it survives); `reconcileCardKeys` moves open/editing/order keys when a category is renamed anywhere (Saved Categories too) and forgets deleted ones, all at once from the state as it was (`remapCardKeys`; one at a time, in a dictionary's order, deleting the first of two same-named cards could close the second). Opening a card that isn't first in its row moves it to the row's start only for show (`categoryDisplayOrder`): leaving Edit and sort changes re-lay out open cards (`reopenCards`), and a drag saves only the dragged card's move (`savedOrder`). Columns use the window's size (`WindowSizeReader`), which keyboards don't change.
 - **Bottom bar**: no bar of its own; Settings (glass circle, left), the week selector (glass capsule, center) and Edit/Done as text (glass capsule, right) float above the home indicator, each with its own Liquid Glass (`BarBackground`; Done is tinted green). The selector's middle button opens the calendar sheet: a plain calendar, or with calendar events on a green `calendar.and.person`. Retro keeps its bordered boxes instead of glass. Each side is as wide as the wider of Edit and Done (`editSideWidth`, measured from both words laid out hidden), the Settings side copying it, so the selector stays centered and its arrows get their full 44pt on every iPhone (sides sized for two buttons left them ~30pt on an SE). The words stop growing at xxxLarge (`editLabel`'s `.dynamicTypeSize`): at the largest sizes they squeezed the arrows to 28pt. Taps between the buttons reach the cards. The grid's bottom padding follows the row's measured height.
-- **Edit mode (bottom bar)**: category management — add-category card and delete badges, with a "Hold and drag a card to move it" hint; open cards collapse (and reopen when editing ends) and can't open meanwhile. A card's own edit button edits only that card's tasks (trash cans, renaming). Deleting a category removes it from the viewed week and all later weeks (earlier weeks keep it; a future week records it in `dismissedCategories` so syncing doesn't add it back) and keeps its saved template.
-- **Card sort** (Settings ▸ Categories ▸ Sort Cards, `store.categorySort`): Manual (hold and drag), Recently Edited First, or Least Recently Edited First (never-edited cards count as oldest: last, or first). Edit times are per category name in UserDefaults (`categoryEditTimes`, set by `noteEdit` in every task mutation and by adding a category; renames carry them; names no longer used are pruned at launch). The setting is stored as a raw string, so an unknown value reads as Manual. ContentView applies a snapshot (`sortedNames`) refreshed only on launch, return from the background (not Notification Center), week change, leaving Edit, setting change, or when every card is closed (a renamed card keeps its place), so cards never jump while being used; card dragging is off unless Manual.
